## Read GraphQL and MCP find through the graph-cache companions

Context: Explorer Preview/Expansion already read the `_entity_search`,
`_adj_out`/`_adj_in`, and `_props` companion tables instead of the
reader-facing SPO relation. GraphQL's typed list/nested-field resolvers and
MCP's `describe_entity` / `/triples/find` find-and-traverse path did not —
every call rescanned the live union relation. This change makes both read
the same companions when ready, with an exact fallback to the previous SQL
when a companion is missing or a missing-table error occurs mid-query.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/entity_search.py
   Add `entity_search_uri_search_sql` (exact-type-URI match, for GraphQL/
   Preview-style callers) and `entity_search_seed_sql` (local-name-suffix
   type match, for MCP find-style callers), both built on a newly extracted
   `_entity_search_text_clause` helper. Add `is_missing_relation_error`,
   extracted from `find_preview_seeds`'s existing fallback detection.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/adjacency.py
   Add `seeded_bfs_sql`, a leveled adjacency BFS seeded from an arbitrary
   subquery instead of a fixed URI list, returning `(entity, min_lvl)` rows.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py
   `find_subjects_by_type`, `get_triples_for_subjects`, and `bfs_traversal`
   each gain a companion-aware branch gated by `entity_search_ready` /
   `adjacency_ready` / `supports_props`, falling back to the exact previous
   SQL when the companion is not ready or a missing-table error occurs.
4. docs/optimizations.md, docs/architecture.md
   Document the new companion-aware read paths and the two `entity_type`
   matching modes (full-URI exact vs. local-name suffix) that predate this
   change and remain unchanged.

