## Route all Analytics job SQL through the Build warehouse

Context: Knowledge Graph Analytics mixed the Lakehouse query warehouse into
the job path. The preflight probe and, after a successful Databricks job, its
result readback could therefore send Thrift SQL to Lakehouse/RT. Every SQL
operation belonging to Analytics jobs now uses the shared Build warehouse
client contract; the Lakehouse query warehouse is never resolved.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graph_analysis/preflight.py
   Probe the mapped-triples source through the Build warehouse client.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobMetrics.py
   Materialize and drop disposable Analytics snapshots through the Build warehouse.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   Read job output and exhaustive metric series through the Build warehouse builder instead of constructing query-warehouse clients.
4. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_analytics.py
   Require the Analytics preflight to request the Build warehouse.
5. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_metric_series.py
   Require metric-series SQL to use the Build warehouse client.
6. tests/units/core/test_job_metrics.py
   Require temporary snapshot DDL to use the Build warehouse client.
7. tests/units/dtwin/test_analytics_job_status.py
   Route probe outcome fixtures through the shared builder contract.
8. tests/units/dtwin/test_dtwin_analytics.py
   Add a regression test that rejects query-warehouse construction during job result readback.

