## Translate SWRL built-ins during inference

Context: The "Customer with active contract owns meter" rule returned no
inferences even though Anna Martin has two active contracts linked to five
meters. The inference translator treated `swrlb:contains` as a graph property
instead of applying its SQL string predicate.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLSQLTranslator.py
   Exclude built-ins from graph joins and apply them as filters after antecedent variables are bound.
2. tests/units/ontology/test_swrl_engine.py
   Add a regression test requiring `swrlb:contains` to produce a SQL filter rather than a nonexistent property join.

